Hi @Kikobeats,

That's because the label is directly the string "25 <= price <=282" and for the `Range`, there's no child to display contrary to the `Refinement List`.

If this structure is not what you want, you can use the [`connectCurrentRefinements`](https://community.algolia.com/instantsearch.js/react/connectors/connectCurrentRefinements.html) connector to define your own. By using the connector, you will have access to the prop `items` that have a structure like: 

```json
[{
    "attributeName": "category",
    "label": "category: ",
    "currentRefinement": ["Sails"],
    "items": [{
        "label": "Sails"
    }]
}, {
    "label": "4.99 <= price <= 699",
    "currentRefinement": {
        "min": 4.99,
        "max": 699
    },
    "attributeName": "price"
}]
```
